      "content": "Sure, I can help you outline these resident profiles. \n\n**Long-term Resident (Older Part of the Neighborhood):**\n\nDaily Routine and Social Habits: \n- Wake up and walk their dog in the neighborhood park, chatting with familiar faces along the way.\n- Stop by the small, local bakery to pick up breakfast, chatting with the owner who recognizes them instantly.\n- Work from home, using the porch as an office space while neighbors greet them.\n- Retire afternoons often spent gardening, inviting neighbors for occasional brief social interactions.\n- Evening walks are spent talking to people they know, whether it’s about day’s events or sharing jokes.\n- Utilizes public spaces at irregular hours, maintaining a life defined by long-standing, albeit informal, community bonds.\n\n**Newcomer (Recently Moved In):**\n\nDaily Routine and Social Habits:\n- Early mornings often spent setting up their home and settling in, unfamiliar faces make new neighbors an unfamiliarity at first.\n- Quickly learns the importance of a gym membership, valuing personal health and intentionally dedicating time for it, though feeling slightly isolated.\n- Work from home but is still polite but somewhat reserved, mindful of how neighbors perceive a new arrival.\n- Evening time is often spent on online",
